# people-graph reads exactly one environment variable, and it is optional.
# There are no secrets, API keys or tokens in this app: never put any in this file.
# Either export it in the shell (PEOPLE_DB=... npx next dev) or copy this file to .env.local,
# which Next.js loads on start. .env* files other than this template are git-ignored.

# Path of the people SQLite file. Default when unset: ~/.openclaw/data/people.sqlite
# The app WRITES to this file (validated CRUD), so point it at a scratch DB when developing.
# Seed one with: python3 ~/.openclaw/skills/people-graph/people_write.py --db /tmp/seed.sqlite init
# PEOPLE_DB=/tmp/seed.sqlite
